// Timeline of Progress: the curated canon of breakthroughs (input to build-progress.mjs).
// The selection is informed by the standard histories of science; every fact shown on the page (people, dates,
// institutions, places, coordinates, descriptions) comes from Wikidata (CC0). Titles and notes here are PRP's own
// short wording. Nothing is taken from any copyrighted reference work.
//
// One entry per breakthrough:
//   id  stable slug (used in links: science/progress/#y=<year>&e=<id>)
//   y   year (negative = BC);  ca: 1 when the date is approximate
//   d   disciplines, the first is the main one (its colour): astro phys chem bio med earth math tech
//   t   title (own wording)                       n   one-sentence note (own wording)
//   q   Wikidata item of the discovery/invention  w   its English Wikipedia title (used to resolve and check q)
//   p   people: "Q<id> English Wikipedia title"; the first is the principal discoverer
//   at  curated place, overriding the automatic rules (only where Wikidata's facts would mislead)
//   fb  fallback place, used only when no rule finds a location
// A name without a QID is resolved through English Wikipedia at build time (and logged); a QID whose label does not
// match its name is corrected or dropped (and logged).
